cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jspassgen-mcp in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jspassgen-mcp: a local stdio MCP server for jspassgen"
abstract: >-
  A local Model Context Protocol server that lets AI assistants generate
  passwords with jspassgen over stdio, from the operating system's
  CSPRNG, without logging the result. It adds no generation logic of its
  own.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
version: "0.0.23"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
# Dual-licensed, at the user's option (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT).
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/jspassgen-mcp"
url: "https://jspassgen.com"
keywords:
  - password
  - password-generator
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - csprng
  - JavaScript
